(text "RASPBERRY PI 5 DOMAIN  (relays, presence sensors, RTC)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 16.51 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "350c1046-cd7f-4ae6-a050-caad21801689"))
(text "ESP32 DOMAIN  (11x PZEM-004T via 2x CD74HC4067 at 5V, level converter, 2x aircon IR)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 149.86 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "45f05792-7ac6-4882-8c6f-8de9106e58b0"))
(text "WIRING NOTES\n1. Same label name = same wire. Connect every pin that shares a label.\n   Full pin-to-pin list: NETLIST.md\n2. J1 pin numbers are PHYSICAL header pins (not BCM).\n3. K1 relay board: REMOVE the VCC/JD-VCC jumper.\n   VCC = Pi 3V3 (opto LEDs); JD-VCC + GND = PS1 (5V >=2A).\n   Do NOT tie Pi GND to K1 GND (keeps opto isolation).\n4. Relays are active-LOW: GPIO LOW = relay ON.\n   RLY01-03 drive the PFC capacitor-bank contactors.\n5. GPIO14/15 (HLK zones 1-2) are UART pins:\n   disable serial console + serial hardware.\n6. Keep SPI (GPIO7-11) and audio/PWM overlays\n   (GPIO12/13/18/19) disabled.\n7. Boot check: GPIO9-27 pull down at power-up, so relays\n   may click ON until app.py starts. Fix if needed:\n   config.txt: gpio=9-13,16-24,27=op,dh\n8. PZEM TTL '5V' pins, both mux VCC and the IR modules\n   run on 5V (ESP32 VIN = USB_5V). The ESP32 is 3.3V, so\n   RX/TX pass through the level converter U22 (LV1/LV2).\n9. Two muxes, same S0-S3 wires: Mux A sends the selected\n   PZEM TX to ESP32 RX1, Mux B sends ESP32 TX1 to that\n   PZEM RX only. Channel Cn = PZEM #n on BOTH muxes.\n10. Both mux EN = GND (always on). C11-C15 unused.\n11. Control wiring only: mains side not shown." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 299.72 16.51 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f6d0f7ae-2e74-4861-9b00-7aef0e55957d"))
(text "MUX WIRING  (2x CD74HC4067, Mux A + Mux B)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 299.72 76.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9b759cc4-e315-496c-b0cb-5ba034685bc7"))
(text "Mux pin\nS0\nS1\nS2\nS3\nSIG\nVCC\nGND\nEN\nC0-C10\nC11-C15" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 299.72 82.55 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "41349145-db47-436f-a096-fac8d56f319a"))
(text "Mux A (U7)\nESP32 GPIO25\nESP32 GPIO26\nESP32 GPIO27\nESP32 GPIO32\nU22 HV1 (GPIO19 RX)\nESP32 5V (VIN)\nESP32 GND\nGND\nTX of PZEM #0-#10\nopen" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 322.58 82.55 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c2aa581b-f7c1-4f86-a314-d0edc683bfdf"))
(text "Mux B (U19)\nESP32 GPIO25  (same wire)\nESP32 GPIO26  (same wire)\nESP32 GPIO27  (same wire)\nESP32 GPIO32  (same wire)\nU22 HV2 (GPIO18 TX)\nESP32 5V (VIN)\nESP32 GND\nGND\nRX of PZEM #0-#10\nopen" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 361.95 82.55 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d14aead3-516e-40e0-8e7b-b93814b56668"))
(text "- S0-S3, VCC and GND go to BOTH muxes: one wire from the ESP32,\n  then jump Mux A S0 -> Mux B S0 (or split it with a Y splice).\n  Same for S1, S2, S3, VCC, GND/EN. Only SIG is different.\n- Channel Cn = PZEM #n on BOTH muxes: its TX on Mux A Cn,\n  its RX on Mux B Cn. Wrong channel = that PZEM shows STANDBY.\n- Both muxes switch together: ESP32 asks PZEM #n through Mux B,\n  PZEM #n answers through Mux A." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 299.72 113.03 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6f4010d6-6893-4701-90a1-cbece9da9d3d"))
(text "LEVEL CONVERTER U22  (4-ch, LV = 3.3V side, HV = 5V side)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 165.1 250.19 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "84dad0f5-a3f7-4c25-8c84-e15c06fd1243"))
